win10xbox: no Wine-only exports that nothing in the builtin set imports

A program that looks for Wine calls GetProcAddress(ntdll, "wine_get_version") (or the other wine_get_*
names). ntdll's wine_get_version, wine_get_build_id and wine_get_host_version and kernel32's
wine_get_unix_file_name and wine_get_dos_file_name are Wine-only exports; of the modules in dlls.txt only
shell32 imported them (the unix trash folder of the recycle bin and the \\?\unix\ display names, both of
which need a unix host that does not exist here). shell32 now answers "no unix counterpart" itself, the five
lines leave the .spec files. user32 and shell32's About box look wine_get_version / wine_get_build_id up
with GetProcAddress and test for NULL, so they need no change.

Not touched: wine_server_call / wine_server_fd_to_handle / wine_server_handle_to_fd (imported by
programs/conhost) and the __wine_* family (imported by kernel32, kernelbase, msvcrt, ucrtbase, or looked up
by name by the layer).

diff --git a/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec b/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec
index 87eb83a..36c0851 100644
--- a/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec
+++ b/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec
@@ -1731,5 +1731,3 @@
 # or 'wine_' (for user-visible functions) to avoid namespace conflicts.
 
 # Unix files
-@ cdecl wine_get_unix_file_name(wstr)
-@ cdecl wine_get_dos_file_name(str)
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/ntdll.spec b/dlls/ntdll/ntdll.spec
index f396c33..931e659 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/ntdll.spec
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/ntdll.spec
@@ -1765,6 +1765,3 @@
 @ cdecl -norelay __wine_dbg_strdup(str)
 
 # Version
-@ cdecl wine_get_version()
-@ cdecl wine_get_build_id()
-@ cdecl wine_get_host_version(ptr ptr)
